    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "The 1‑room West Freehold Schoolhouse on Wemrock Road dates back to the 19th century and once stood on land that was part of the Walker‑Combs‑Hartshorne farm.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://twp.freehold.nj.us/436/History-of-the-Village-of-West-Freehold",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Moore’s Tavern and Restaurant, now a local favorite, began life as Mount’s Tavern on the southwest corner of West Freehold’s Main Street.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://twp.freehold.nj.us/436/History-of-the-Village-of-West-Freehold",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1995, the Freehold Township Committee honored the historic farm that later became Moore’s Inn by designating it a landmark site.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://twp.freehold.nj.us/436/History-of-the-Village-of-West-Freehold",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "West Freehold sits just two miles from the Battle of Monmouth, and its Village Historic District preserves many colonial‑era structures.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Freehold%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Burlington Path, a 17th‑century stagecoach route, once ran through West Freehold, linking Burlington and Perth Amboy.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Freehold%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Long before European settlement, the Lenni Lenape Indians were the original inhabitants of the land that became West Freehold.",
